      "text": "April 2023 Engineering Safety Rule Book - CPKC\nAppendix 2: Personal Protective Equipment and Clothing Charts \nEngineering PPE  \nGeneral Requirements\nR = Required equipment\nX = May be required based \non task and materials\nY = Recommended \nadditional equipment\nAbrasive blasting\n(Sand Blasting)\nRR R R XX\nAdzing Machine \n(Open Cab)\nRR R X Y\nArc Welding XR R X RX Welding jacket required\nBackpack Blower  \n(i.e. Snow or Leaf)\nRR R X\nBallast Dumping (Manual) X R R R Dampen ballast before \ndumping\nBanding Materials RR\nBatteries Handling and/or \nServicing (Wet Cell)\nRRX XR\nBlowing or Cleaning \nwith Compressed Air,\nSteam or Water\nRR R X X\nBoring, Drilling or Reaming \nMetal\nXR R X\nBreaking Frozen \nMaterials (Ice, Ground  \nBallast, etc.) with \nHand T ools\nXR R\nBreaking or Cutting \nConcrete, Stone or Asphalt\nRR R R X\nBrush Cutting RR R X X\n and Polishing with \nWire Wheel\nXR R X\nCad Welding (S&C) X R R X X\nPin Brazing (S&C) XR R X\nCarbon-Arc Cutting and \nGouging\nRR R X RX Double hearing protection \nmay be required\nChain Saw\nRR R\n \n \nChemical Plugger XR R X X Refer to manufacturer \n and SDS as \nthey may require a higher \nlevel of PPE\nChipping, Cutting or  \nCalking Metal\nXR R X XX\nChop Saw RR R X X\nClimbing Poles RR Long sleeve shirts are \nrequired for pole climbing. \nFall protection equipment \nrequired\nCut-Off Disks, Saws or \nOther T ools with Carbide \nBits/Blades\nRR R X X\nHearing Protection\nSee Eye & Face \nProtection Chart\nSee Work\nGlove Chart\nSee Respiratory\nProtection Chart\nWelders Jacket  or\nSleeves\nSpats Leggings\nDisposable Overalls\nRubberized Apron/\nLab Coat\nRemarks\nApproved chainsaw chaps,\nleggings or pants. Cut \nresistant arm and shoulder \nprotection required for \noverhead chainsaw use.\n \n49",
