      "id": "cpkc_eng_safety_rule_book_april_2023_english_p62_b0",
      "title": "At CPKC we are all Leaders, no matter our job title or the color of hard hat we …",
      "text": "At CPKC we are all Leaders, no matter our job title or the color of hard hat we wear.   \nAs a Leader, you  team performance and results by modeling and shaping behaviors which \nthe safe behaviors within your teams! \nLeadership is also about the ability to inspire, develop and engage individuals and teams by creating \na positive, respectful work environment where people want to perform by:  \n \n• Communicating pinpointed expectations; without  direction/job planning, \nor detailed job  it makes it  to execute the work safely and    \n• Observing and validating behaviors; REMEMBER your Home Safe commitment  \n“if you see a co-worker at risk you will warn them” or “give a heads up”.  We cannot  \ndo that if we are not watching out for each other and communicating.\n• Engaging and empowering employees effectively; by providing a balance between \nto give each other feedback so we can achieve world class results together, the safe way. \nCPKC Home Safe   \nCommitment\n• I don’t want to be injured\n• If I am at risk I want a co-worker to let me know\n• I don’t want a co-worker injured\n• If I see a co-worker at risk I will warn them\nAction\n• Give a heads up\n• Offer and ask for support (help)\n• Warn people who you believe are putting themselves or others at risk\n• Identify, report and remove hazards\nLeadership the CPKC Way\ndirectly impact CPKC’s safety culture. Positive reinforcement is the most effective way to get a \nperson to repeat the same behavior . Remember to look for opportunities to positively reinforce \nboth positive and constructive feedback. Leadership the CPKC Way means we care enough",
      "order": 61,
      "parent_id": null,
      "source_ref": {
        "page": 62,
        "label": "Page 62"
      }
    },
