      "id": "cpkc_te_safety_rule_book_april_2023_p3_b0",
      "title": "The FAB 4",
      "text": "The FAB 4\nFour principles of proper body mechanics \nthat help keep you safe at work and home. \nContract \nyour \nShoulders\n4\nBend at  \nthe hips\n3\n1\n Wide stance \nBend at  \nthe knees\n2\nAction\n• Give a heads up \n• Offer and ask for support (help) \n•  Warn people I believe are at risk\n•  Identify, report, and remove hazards\nMutual Respect Partnering Coaching\nHome Safe\n™\n starts here\n100% Compliance Accountability Courage\nIt is a commitment to be vigilant about \npersonal safety and the safety of co-workers.\nNatural Instincts (Dependent)\nSelf (Independent)\nTeam\nSupervision\nManagement \nCommitment\nPersonal\nCommitment\nTeam \nCommitment\n(Interdependent)\n(Control)\n(Acceptance)\n(Compliance)\n(Commitment)\n(Dedication)AT-RISK BEHAVIOURS DRIVE OUTCOMES AT THE TOP\nFatality\nTOTAL RECORDABLE RATE\n(Edict)\n4.0\n3.0\n2.5\n2.0\n1.5\n1.0\n0.5\n1\n30\n300\nLost Workday\nCases\nRecorded Injuries\n3,000\nNear Misses (Est.)\n3,000,000\nAt-Risk Behaviours (Est.)\nCommitment\n• I don’t want to be injured \n•  If I am at risk I expect a co-worker to let me know \n•  I don’t want a co-worker injured \n•  I have the courage to speak up if I see a hazard or someone at risk\nStarting with the first minute every day, my:\nThroughout every day, I will:",
      "order": 2,
